{
  "why": [
    "One list, executed by both implementations, so a divergence is a real one",
    "rather than two hand-written scripts that drifted. Each case is a sequence",
    "of BeliefEngine.update calls against one shared belief store; the store is",
    "serialised afterwards and compared field by field, bit for bit.",
    "",
    "The cases are chosen for the ways a port goes wrong, not for coverage:",
    "repetition from one origin, independent corroboration, contradiction",
    "across the three kinds, an integer origin id that JSON turns into a string,",
    "the provenance trim, and extremes where a naive sigmoid overflows."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "one_origin_repeated",
      "why": "The correlation discount. Twenty hearings of one rumour must saturate near the 1/(1-rho) ceiling, not approach certainty.",
      "updates": [
        {"repeat": 20, "predicate": "was_at",
         "slots": {"agent": "agent:vee", "place": "place:clinic", "when": 1200},
         "polarity": "+", "trust": 0.6, "competence": 0.5, "skepticism": 0.1,
         "claim_id": "claim:rumour", "origin": 4711, "world_time": 1200,
         "speaker": "agent:byrne"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "independent_corroboration",
